# Test: the BUILT le binary runs the consistency gate over the real checkout,
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
#       gives the same answer independently of the working directory, and
#       exposes the same findings as structured data.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-le-is-a-ze-binary AC-11 over the REAL TREE, and AC-7 for the
#            first ported tool, against the artifact a developer runs.
# PREVENTS: a consistency implementation that passes focused fixtures but
#           disagrees with the real checkout, changes with the current working
#           directory, or exposes a different payload through row operators.
#
# The registered fixture compiles cmd/ze as le into its own temporary directory,
# so no build artifact is written back into the checkout. Report comparisons are
# over the multiset of lines because ordering is not part of the report contract.
#
# The timeout is declared because the fixture performs a cold product build and
# several full walks of the real checkout.

option=timeout:value=300s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture ui/le-consistency-answers
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
